Set up Saltvoice Local on this Windows PC. It is the offline build: local Whisper speech-to-text, then paste into Grok Bot. No API key.

This is not the API Saltvoice repo. Do not mix the two.

1. Confirm Python 3.11+ is installed and on PATH (`python --version`). If not, tell me to install it from python.org with “Add python.exe to PATH” and stop.
2. Clone https://github.com/GeorgieXRPL/saltvoice-local into C:\Users\<ME>\saltvoice-local (use my real Windows username). The repo is private — use gh or git with my existing GitHub login.
3. If a folder named Saltvoice (the API app) is already running, close it first. Do not run Saltvoice and Saltvoice Local at the same time.
4. Copy config.example.yaml to config.yaml if config.yaml does not exist. There is no .env and no XAI_API_KEY. Do not invent keys.
5. Keep the Grok Bot window open. Saltvoice Local finds it by title (Grok Bot / Grok / Grok Build) and pastes transcribed text into it.
6. Run run.bat once and keep that console open. First run creates a venv, installs packages, and downloads the Whisper model into %LOCALAPPDATA%\SaltvoiceLocal\models (about 75 MB). Later runs are offline. If ctranslate2 fails, tell me to install the VC++ redistributable, then stop.
7. Confirm a window titled Saltvoice Local appears at the top of the screen. If not, look on the taskbar or press Ctrl+Alt+H.
8. Then tell me:
   - Start: say “Salt open voice over” (also “Salt start voice over” or Ctrl+Alt+G)
   - Speak a task; it should appear as text in this Grok Bot chat
   - Stop: say “Salt stop voice over”
   - Ctrl+Alt+X quits listening; Ctrl+Alt+H shows the overlay
9. Log file (no secrets): %LOCALAPPDATA%\SaltvoiceLocal\saltvoice-local.log

If something fails, append what you saw to WINDOWS-FEEDBACK.md (create it if missing), commit, and push. Do not print API keys. Do not commit .env files from the other Saltvoice folder.
